  dyck-1                            0.6759    0.6931    0.18        1.03 x
  periodic                          0.0055    5.5452    0.01     1013.86 x
  copy                              2.3475    5.5452    0.44        2.36 x
  counting_anbn                     0.1666    5.5452    0.08       33.28 x
  counting_anbncn                   0.1134    5.5452    0.08       48.92 x
  interleaving                      0.0027    5.5452    0.01     2048.00 x
  permutation_cycle                 0.0047    5.5452    0.01     1175.32 x
  hierarchical                      0.0041    5.5452    0.01     1365.00 x
  random                            5.5452    5.5452    1.01        1.00 x
  identity                          0.0014    5.5452    0.01     4096.00 x
  composite_mirror_repeat           1.3863    5.5452    0.52        4.00 x
  mixer 🔮 ⚠️                       0.4855    5.5452    0.17       11.42 x
  nca (learnable_50)                1.0052    2.0794    0.30        2.07 x

  Oracle Loss    Best possible cross-entropy — a perfect model that learned the rule.
  Random         Cross-entropy of a uniform random guesser = ln(vocab size).
  Gzip Ratio     gzip compressed size ÷ raw size.  Lower = more structured / redundant.
  Improvement    Random ÷ Oracle.  How many times better than random guessing.
                 Values near 1.0 -> little or no learnable signal in the data.
  🔮             Oracle value is a LOOSE lower bound; true floor is higher.
  ⚠️             See Diagnostic Checks section below.

